</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Under
the Local Government Act 1976, a local authority is empowered to issue licenses or permits for various trades, occupations, or premises.
These licenses can be granted with specific conditions and restrictions determined by the local authority. Typically, businesses are
required to obtain such licenses when they occupy office spaces for their operations or when they install signboards.</span></p><div>

