interest in a subsidiary is accounted for separately from the parent&#8217;s ownership interests in a subsidiary. Profit or loss and
each component of other comprehensive income are attributed to the shareholders of the parent and non-controlling interest, even if this
result in the non-controlling interest having a deficit balance. A change in the ownership interest of a subsidiary without a loss of
control, is accounted for as an equity transaction.</span></p></ix:continuation>

