are measured on either of the following bases:</span></p></ix:continuation>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<ix:continuation continuedAt="yygh_DescriptionOfAccountingPolicyForExpectedCreditLosses-c0_cont_5" id="yygh_DescriptionOfAccountingPolicyForExpectedCreditLosses-c0_cont_4"><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; width: 100%; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="vertical-align: top; text-align: justify">
<td style="width: 1in"/><td style="width: 0.25in; text-align: left"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#9679;</span></td><td style="text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">12-month
ECLs: these are ECLs that result from default events that are possible within the 12 months after the reporting date (or for a shorter
